# 高频词汇 List01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List01核心词汇

{{account}}{/əˈkaʊnt/}{账户；描述；解释}{She gave a detailed account of what happened.}}
{{achieve}}{/əˈtʃiːv/}{实现；达到}{Hard work and dedication help you achieve your goals.}}
{{adapt}}{/əˈdæpt/}{适应；改编}{Businesses must adapt to changing market conditions.}}
{{address}}{/əˈdres/}{地址；演讲；解决}{The government needs to address the housing crisis.}}
{{adopt}}{/əˈdɒpt/}{采用；收养}{More companies are adopting flexible work arrangements.}}
{{advance}}{/ədˈvɑːns/}{前进；进步；预先的}{Technological advance has transformed the healthcare industry.}}
{{affect}}{/əˈfekt/}{影响；感动}{Climate change affects every aspect of our lives.}}
{{afford}}{/əˈfɔːd/}{负担得起；提供}{Many young people cannot afford to buy a home.}}
{{appeal}}{/əˈpiːl/}{呼吁；上诉；吸引力}{The policy has broad appeal across party lines.}}
{{apply}}{/əˈplaɪ/}{应用；申请；适用}{These principles apply to both individuals and organizations.}}
{{approach}}{/əˈprəʊtʃ/}{方法；接近}{We need a more holistic approach to healthcare.}}
{{appropriate}}{/əˈprəʊpriət/}{适当的；恰当的}{The response was appropriate given the circumstances.}}
{{argue}}{/ˈɑːɡjuː/}{争论；主张}{Scientists argue that immediate action is necessary.}}
{{assess}}{/əˈses/}{评估；评定}{We need to assess the risks before making a decision.}}
{{assign}}{/əˈsaɪn/}{分配；指派}{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{associate}}{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt/}{联想；联合}{People often associate the brand with quality.}}
{{assume}}{/əˈsjuːm/}{假设；承担}{We should not assume that everyone agrees with us.}}
{{attribute}}{/əˈtrɪbjuːt/}{归因于；属性}{The success was attributed to the team's hard work.}}
{{available}}{/əˈveɪləbl/}{可用的；有空的}{Free parking is available for all guests.}}
{{aware}}{/əˈweər/}{意识到的；知道的}{Consumers are becoming more aware of sustainability issues.}}
{{benefit}}{/ˈbenɪfɪt/}{利益；好处}{Regular exercise has numerous health benefits.}}
{{capable}}{/ˈkeɪpəbl/}{有能力的；能干的}{The new system is capable of processing millions of records.}}
{{capacity}}{/kəˈpæsəti/}{能力；容量}{The hospital expanded its capacity to treat more patients.}}
{{challenge}}{/ˈtʃælɪndʒ/}{挑战；质疑}{The team rose to the challenge and delivered excellent results.}}
{{claim}}{/kleɪm/}{声称；索取}{The company claims its product is environmentally friendly.}}
{{commit}}{/kəmˈmɪt/}{犯（罪）；承诺}{The government committed to achieving net-zero emissions.}}
{{communicate}}{/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/}{沟通；传达}{Effective communication is essential in the workplace.}}
{{community}}{/kəˈmjuːnəti/}{社区；群体}{The local community came together to support the cause.}}
{{compare}}{/kəmˈpeər/}{比较；对比}{You cannot compare the two situations directly.}}
{{compete}}{/kəmˈpiːt/}{竞争；比赛}{Small businesses struggle to compete with large corporations.}}
